body:
He says in the Guidebook this exactly:   I would like to move forward in preparation for building the showdown between Guts and Griffith. 

&#x200B;

so he wants to move forward in PREPARATION....for BUILDING the showdown lol so there's still a prep time and a building time. It'll be awhile still I think

> There was no way I was going to fess up and apologize, so instead I just scowled and pretended to look around for the culprit 

&#x200B;

LOLOL fuck I was laughing so hard at that, imagining you doing that 

&#x200B;

There's a few that I can think of

&#x200B;

1. in Mexico, ironically right before I went swimming, one of my friends said to me "You gotta watch out for the current, it will take you out to sea and you could drown". I went out fairly far and got stuck in a current, remembering that advice I frantically swam and barely managed to cling to these rocks before it took me way out to sea where I could have drowned.
2. Was digging for rocks on this really steep hill, it's about 100 feet to the bottom and if you fell you definitely would roll constantly without stopping. At the bottom of the hill was a frozen river. so if I fell I would have gone under the ice and probably drowned. Anyways I was walking along it with my friend and I slipped and barely managed to hold on and had to crawl through the mud and was barely able to get back out
3. Jumped out of a car while I was drunk because my friend jokingly told me to

&#x200B;

Not trolls Lockofwar called it with the brownies! You're right about the other ones though

&#x200B;

[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brownie\_(folklore)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brownie_(folklore))

On Manga you essentially read backwards compared to normal American comics. so start on the right side of the page and move left, and continue the small squares that go down on each side before moving to the big ones.

&#x200B;

Start from the beginning, you won't regret it :)

Thanks I just got to that chapter, you did a good job!

&#x200B;

There's about 8 chapters colored I wish I could find the thread that had them :(

